A||||11||batboy||Sluppy, air dam question||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||03-12-2000||01:26 AM||||Sluppy, I was shipped a DGP air dam with driving light cutouts that looks just like the one on your silver 85 SE. There was no mounting hardware or instructions, how did you attach your air dam? How did you mount your driving lights and what kind are they? Anyone else with that style air dam, feel free to answer also.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||03-12-2000||01:32 PM||||Could you post a picture? I would like to see one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||03-12-2000||02:30 PM||||Does it look like it might fit on a Formula or 87-88 coupe style front?||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||03-12-2000||04:05 PM||||This front air dam will only fit the older coupe style nose, not the GT aero nose. I don't know about the Formula. Do you want to see a pic before it's mounted onto the car? Here's Sluppy's silver Fiero that has either the same front air dam or one just like it.<P> <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/blkwht2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mwbackus||03-12-2000||07:39 PM||||With the newer coupe/formula front being so similar to the pre87, it just seemed possible that it would fit.  I guess one would actually have to check it with a model from those years.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||03-12-2000||08:34 PM||||I don't have access to a Formula right now or I'd try a trial mock-up prior to mounting it onto my own car. Hey Paul H., don't you have a Formula project you're working on? If so, he's not far from me.<P>Mike, since the air dam is just fiberglass anyway, I'm sure any minor differences could be either trimmed or bonded over with body filler. It mounts along the bottom and the Formula looks similar to my 85 SE on this lower edge.<P>Sluppy, I need your help. Where are you?<P>Anyone else have any ideas for lights? The openings are 3.5" X 7". Fog lights or driving lights?<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||sluppy123||03-12-2000||10:05 PM||||Batboy- Sorry for not answering sooner but I've been out gathering parts for the grand-am brake swap.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Here's a pic showing where the mounting screws are.     <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=1876291&p=17733751&Sequence=0" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=247832&a=1876291&p=17733751&Sequence=0</A>  there are a total of 10 screws holding it on. the six screws on the front go through the airdam and bumper into a piece aluminum backing(mine has a lip on the top of it that follows the contour on the underside of the nose.) These are a big pain in the ass to put on, you have to stick your arm up into the nose, then try to get the screws into the holes in the aluminum strip.<P>The center portion of mine has grooves cut into it that rest on the plastic grill up by the radiator. <P>The ends of the airdam extend into the wheel wells and the two bottom screws hold it on.<P>I used a pair of off-Road lights made by Blazer, They fit the hole perfectly.(I got tham at Advanced Auto) I used a piece of aluminum under each light to back up the fiberglass.<P>I hope this helps. LMK if you need anything else<BR>-Brian    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by sluppy123 (edited 03-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||03-12-2000||11:33 PM||||Yes the air dam will fit the Formula/88 coupe front end. Althougt the front ends look different they are very very close on the bottom. A friend has an 84 he made into a convertable and is putting on the 87/88 coupe front end with the DGP air dam. He's hoping to finish it by summer. He's also adding the IMSA spoiler and a V-8.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mwbackus||03-12-2000||11:53 PM||||Kewl, I think Im gonna have to get me one of these airdams then. <P>Thanks,<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||03-13-2000||07:39 AM||||Thanks Sluppy! Did your's come with mounting hardware or did you have to figure it out?||||reg||1
Z||000010||sluppy123||03-13-2000||05:25 PM||||Batboy- Mine came with the aluminum strips that go up in the nose. They are about 13" X 1" x 1/8". Does yours have any mounting holes drilled in it? <P>-Brian<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||batboy||03-13-2000||10:47 PM||||No holes drilled, no mounting strips, no screws, no instructions. Maybe I should call FOCOA tomorrow and see if they just forgot to ship the mounting accessories with the air dam. In case I have to make those backing plates, were there two of them with three holes in each?||||reg||1
